# Tangerine Compiler — Semantic Evolution Plans
# (third-audit item 48, evolution-plan family)
# Self-hosting compiler written in Tangerine
#
# SCOPE. Audit item 48's full subject is an evolution-plan family (plan
# synthesis, plan application, plan validation). The first slice
# (semantic_planning.tg) implemented the well-defined program-knowledge
# machinery (write/read sets, effect resources, risk vectors, memory facts,
# merge risk). THIS module implements the EVOLUTION-PLAN FAMILY: four
# compiler-owned plan records derived purely from existing semantic
# artifacts — the §29 SemanticSnapshot, the §31 SemanticDelta, the §32
# SemanticIndex and the third-audit item-18 typed dependency graph — plus
# the bridge that turns each plan's breaking items into the §36
# ChangeBudget's allowed-delta set entries.
#
# NOTHING here executes a runtime action, synthesizes an edit, applies an
# edit or claims an application: every value is a pure, deterministic
# projection of the snapshot / delta rows a caller supplies. The plans are
# ADVISORY records — the verdict words are the documented compatibility
# rules below, and the budget mapping is the executable link to §36 (a
# plan's items become allowance rows; `budget_verify` stays the gate).
#
# THE FOUR PLANS AND THEIR SOURCES:
#   1. EnumEvolutionPlan (enum_evolution_plan) — one enum type key + one
#      §31 delta: added/removed variants, reordering and the match /
#      discriminant risks. The before variant set comes from the delta's
#      typed carriers (the abi_surfaces per-surface BEFORE row text — the
#      "type:<old key>" surface id IS the old canonical type key — then the
#      public-api before rows); the after set comes from the snapshot's
#      type row: the stable key's "enum{...}" render parsed in declaration
#      order, UNIONed with the ABI type row's already-typed variant field
#      list (the same typed-first union semantic_index.tg documents).
#      Reordering = same set, different declaration order (the signature
#      render preserves declaration order; the index accessors sort, so the
#      plan parses the row render instead of the sorted index answer).
#   2. SignatureEvolutionPlan (signature_evolution_plan) — two snapshots
#      and one function key: the parameter / return / convention diff and
#      the typed callers. The canonical signature text (the "#" component
#      of the symbol row key) IS the protocol carrier, so the parameter and
#      return projections render-diff it — with balanced-paren parsing, not
#      a split. The ABI fn row is PREFERRED where it exists: ownership_in is
#      the typed convention source and ret_class an additional return
#      signal. The caller list is derived from TYPED edges (the §32 index's
#      callers map, itself a fold of the snapshot's call rows), never from
#      text.
#   3. TraitEvolutionPlan (trait_evolution_plan) — two snapshots and one
#      trait key: added/removed methods (the trait row's "trait{...}"
#      render), the impl rows and the risky impls. The typed
#      TraitImplEdge / TraitSelectionEdge rows are the obligation graph:
#      an added method whose name no selected impl method covers makes the
#      impl risky. Added methods with existing impls lacking them =
#      breaking (the immovable obligations); removed methods = review.
#   4. CapabilityPropagationPlan (capability_propagation_plan) — one
#      snapshot + one delta: the effect/capability rows that newly introduce
#      a §11 class or a capability id (the "changed" row keys), the
#      transitive CALLERS reached through the §32 callers index, and the
#      frontier rows where the walk stopped (an Unknown indirect call row
#      in a reached function, or a caller outside the analyzed program).
#      Verdict review whenever anything changed.
#
# DOCUMENTED VERDICT RULES:
#   EnumEvolutionPlan:
#     breaking   — a variant was removed (a match naming it fails) OR the
#                  variant order changed (positional construction and the
#                  variant discriminant / layout order are assumptions the
#                  compiler's own layout engine reads declaration order
#                  for).
#     review     — variants were added AND the type has dependent
#                  functions (recorded typed TypeUse users that are
#                  functions / have MIR summary rows): an addition is
#                  compatible UNLESS a dependent match is exhaustive —
#                  exhaustiveness is not a snapshot fact, so dependents
#                  fail to review. With no dependents the addition is
#                  compatible.
#     compatible — no variant-set change and no reorder.
#   SignatureEvolutionPlan:
#     breaking   — a parameter was removed or reordered, the return
#                  changed (canonical return render or ABI ret_class), a
#                  convention changed, OR a parameter was added. Added
#                  parameters are fail-closed breaking because the
#                  canonical signature render carries no DEFAULT marker:
#                  a default-carrying addition cannot be proven from these
#                  rows, so every addition is treated as a no-default
#                  addition (breaking for existing callers) and must be
#                  explicitly budgeted. The caller list does not decide
#                  the verdict — a breaking item does not become safe when
#                  the snapshot records no caller (unrecorded/external
#                  callers exist) — but it is always reported.
#     review     — the signature text changed in a dimension this plan
#                  does not classify (today: the declared-effect id suffix
#                  the snapshot render appends after the return type).
#     compatible — the canonical signature text and every typed mirror
#                  agree.
#   TraitEvolutionPlan:
#     breaking   — a method was added and at least one existing impl does
#                  not select it (the immovable obligation: every impl must
#                  grow the method, and the render carries no default-method
#                  marker, so an addition is fail-closed an obligation).
#     review     — methods were added with no risky impl (no obligation
#                  exists) or methods were removed (remaining selections /
#                  call sites need review).
#     compatible — no method change.
#   CapabilityPropagationPlan:
#     review     — anything changed (a capability / effect addition always
#                  crosses a call-graph boundary).
#     compatible — no addition.
#
# DETERMINISM. Every list this module returns is sorted by byte order and
# deduped through the first slice's planning_sorted_keys (parameter lists
# keep exact multiplicity: the multiset diff sorts but never collapses two
# identical parameter renders). Declaration-order variant lists are the
# documented exception (order IS the reorder signal) and are rendered
# through the same parser on both sides. No Map iteration order, insertion
# order or hash order ever reaches a result.
#
# TABLE OF CONTENTS:
#   1. The typed plan records + the EvolutionPlan family enum.
#   2. Shared helpers (key parsing, signature parsing, multiset diff).
#   3. EnumEvolutionPlan (enum_evolution_plan).
#   4. SignatureEvolutionPlan (signature_evolution_plan).
#   5. TraitEvolutionPlan (trait_evolution_plan).
#   6. CapabilityPropagationPlan (capability_propagation_plan).
#   7. The §36 budget mapping (evolution_plan_to_budget_constraints,
#      evolution_plans_to_budget_constraints, evolution_budget_of_
#      constraints, evolution_budget_constraints_of_delta).
#   8. The executable lane rows (semantic_evolution_lane_check and the five
#      sub-lanes). No test-file-only fixtures: the rows are exported
#      functions a behavior lane calls, the semantic_planning.tg sibling
#      style. The lane builds small snapshot pairs through the
#      semantic_delta.tg lane fixtures (delta_lane_snapshot /
#      delta_lane_sid / delta_lane_fn_symbol / delta_lane_type_row) and
#      diffs them through the REAL semantic_delta_of.

use std::collections::{Vec, Map, Set}

use tg_compiler::ids::{DefKind}
use tg_compiler::stable_ids::{
  StableDeclId, stable_decl_of_key, stable_decl_eq,
  stable_key_name_part, stable_key_signature
}
use tg_compiler::semantic_model::{
  SemanticSnapshot, SemanticType, SemanticTypeKind, SemanticSymbol,
  AbiSurfaceRow, CallEdge, CallEdgeKind, IndirectCallEdge,
  SemanticDependencyGraph, TypeUseEdge, TraitImplEdge, TraitSelectionEdge
}
use tg_compiler::semantic_delta::{
  SemanticDelta, EffectDelta, CapabilityDelta, EffectSummaryView, Presence,
  semantic_delta_of, semantic_delta_empty, semantic_delta_rows_diff,
  # The semantic_delta.tg lane fixtures the lane rows build their snapshot
  # pairs through (the semantic_planning.tg lane-style reuse; the symbols
  # are module-visible like semantic_delta_empty, which the first slice
  # already imports).
  delta_lane_snapshot, delta_lane_sid, delta_lane_fn_symbol, delta_lane_type_row
}
use tg_compiler::semantic_index::{
  SemanticIndex, build_semantic_index, index_callers_of, index_symbol_get,
  index_mir_summary_of, index_type_users_of,
  index_brace_body, index_top_level_parts, index_member_name,
  index_abi_member_names
}
use tg_compiler::change_budget::{
  ChangeBudget, budget_verify, budget_public_api_row_key, budget_abi_row_key,
  budget_capability_addition_key, budget_cap_id_of, budget_effect_cap_id_of
}
# The first slice's planning helpers (the SAME determinism boundary and §11
# class vocabulary — reusing them keeps the two item-48 slices on one
# implementation, never two).
use tg_compiler::semantic_planning::{
  planning_keys_add, planning_sorted_keys, planning_text_lists_same,
  planning_key_root, planning_class_bits,
  planning_effect_added_class, planning_effect_added_cap,
  planning_capability_text
}

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 1. THE TYPED PLAN RECORDS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# One enum's variant-set evolution (see the module doc's verdict rules).
#   type_key         — the CURRENT (b-side) full type key
#                      ("path::Name#enum{A(...),B(...)}").
#   added_variants   — variant names present after but not before (sorted).
#   removed_variants — variant names present before but not after (sorted).
#   reordered        — the SAME variant set in a different declaration
#                      order (the signature render / typed field list order
#                      changed).
#   risks            — the documented risk rows, sorted:
#                      "added-variant:<name>:compatible-unless-exhaustive-match",
#                      "removed-variant:<name>:match-may-break",
#                      "reordered-variants:discriminant-assumptions",
#                      "dependent:<fn key>" (one row per dependent function).
#   verdict          — "compatible" | "review" | "breaking" (module doc).
pub struct EnumEvolutionPlan
  type_key: String
  added_variants: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  removed_variants: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  reordered: Bool = false
  risks: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  verdict: String
end

# One function signature's evolution (see the module doc's verdict rules).
#   function          — the current (b-side when it exists) full key text.
#   param_added       — the canonical "conv:type" renders of parameters
#                       present after but not before (multiset difference,
#                       sorted; duplicates preserved).
#   param_removed     — the same for parameters present before but not after.
#   param_reordered   — the same parameter multiset in a different positional
#                       order.
#   return_changed    — the canonical return render changed, OR both sides
#                       carry an ABI fn row whose ret_class differs.
#   convention_changes— positional convention rows "<index>:<old>-><new>",
#                       typed-first from the ABI fn rows' ownership_in, the
#                       parsed param render fallback.
#   callers           — the TYPED callers of the function (the §32 index's
#                       reverse call graph), sorted.
#   verdict           — "compatible" | "review" | "breaking" (module doc).
pub struct SignatureEvolutionPlan
  function: String
  param_added: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  param_removed: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  param_reordered: Bool = false
  return_changed: Bool = false
  convention_changes: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  callers: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  verdict: String
end

# One trait's method-surface evolution (see the module doc's verdict rules).
#   trait_key      — the current (b-side when it exists) full type key.
#   methods_added  — trait method names present after but not before.
#   methods_removed— trait method names present before but not after.
#   impls          — the trait's typed impl rows "self-type|impl-key" (the
#                    TraitImplEdge inverse), sorted.
#   risky_impls    — the impl rows that do not select at least one added
#                    method (the immovable obligations), sorted.
#   verdict        — "compatible" | "review" | "breaking" (module doc).
pub struct TraitEvolutionPlan
  trait_key: String
  methods_added: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  methods_removed: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  impls: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  risky_impls: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  verdict: String
end

# One change's capability / effect propagation over the call graph (see the
# module doc's verdict rules). All lists are sorted and deduped.
#   changed       — the changed capability / effect ROW keys: the function
#                   key of an effect row that newly carries a §11 class,
#                   and the canonical "fn|cap<id>" key of a newly present
#                   capability (a capability edge toggle or an effect-view
#                   capability addition).
#   propagated_to — the transitive CALLERS reached through the §32 callers
#                   index (the changed functions themselves are seeds, not
#                   propagation rows).
#   blocked_at    — the frontier rows where propagation stopped:
#                   "<fn>|unknown-indirect:<site>" for a reached function
#                   carrying an Unknown IndirectCallEdge (the walk does not
#                   expand through it), and "<caller>|external" for a
#                   caller with no symbol and no MIR summary row in the
#                   snapshot (outside the analyzed program; the caller
#                   stays listed in propagated_to but the walk stops
#                   there).
#   verdict       — "review" | "compatible" (module doc).
pub struct CapabilityPropagationPlan
  changed: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  propagated_to: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  blocked_at: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  verdict: String
end

# The evolution-plan FAMILY — one wrapper so a task holds one Vec[EvolutionPlan]
# and the budget mapping takes the whole family in one call.
pub enum EvolutionPlan
  EnumPlan(EnumEvolutionPlan)
  SignaturePlan(SignatureEvolutionPlan)
  TraitPlan(TraitEvolutionPlan)
  CapabilityPlan(CapabilityPropagationPlan)
end

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 2. SHARED HELPERS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The first index of `needle` in `s` at or after `from` (-1 when absent).
def evolution_text_index(s: String, needle: String, from: Int) -> Int
  var i = from
  while i + needle.len() <= s.len() do
    if s.slice(i, i + needle.len()) == needle then
      return i
    end
    i = i + 1
  end
  -1
end

# The LAST index of `needle` in `s` (-1 when absent).
def evolution_last_text_index(s: String, needle: String) -> Int
  var found = -1
  var i = 0
  while i + needle.len() <= s.len() do
    if s.slice(i, i + needle.len()) == needle then
      found = i
    end
    i = i + 1
  end
  found
end

# Sort a text list without deduping (parameter multisets; a reorder probe
# must not collapse duplicate renders).
def evolution_sorted_keep(inout v: Vec[String]) -> Unit
  v.sort_by(|a, b| a < b)
  ()
end

# a - b as a MULTISET: every occurrence of `a` consumes one occurrence of
# `b`; the remainder is sorted (duplicates preserved).
def evolution_multiset_minus(a: Vec[String], b: Vec[String]) -> Vec[String]
  var remaining: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for x in b do
    remaining.push(x.clone())
  end
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for x2 in a do
    var found = -1
    var i = 0
    while i < remaining.len() do
      if found < 0 && remaining[i] == x2 then
        found = i
      end
      i = i + 1
    end
    if found >= 0 then
      remaining.remove(found)
    else
      out.push(x2.clone())
    end
  end
  evolution_sorted_keep(&mut out)
  out
end

# a - b as a SET (both inputs are sorted unique lists; the output is sorted
# unique).
def evolution_set_minus(a: Vec[String], b: Vec[String]) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for x in a do
    if !b.contains(&x) then
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, x.clone())
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# The text after the first occurrence of `sep` ("" when absent).
def evolution_text_after_first(s: String, sep: String) -> String
  let at = evolution_text_index(&s, &sep, 0)
  if at < 0 then "".to_string() else s.slice(at + sep.len(), s.len()) end
end

# The text before the first occurrence of `sep` (the whole text when absent).
def evolution_text_before_first(s: String, sep: String) -> String
  let at = evolution_text_index(&s, &sep, 0)
  if at < 0 then s.clone() else s.slice(0, at) end
end

# The module path of a name-part text: everything before the LAST "::"
# (a top-level name has no module — ""). "a::b::N" -> "a::b".
def evolution_name_module(name: String) -> String
  let at = evolution_last_text_index(&name, "::")
  if at < 0 then "".to_string() else name.slice(0, at) end
end

# The LAST name component after the last "::" ("m::Variant" -> "Variant").
def evolution_name_last(name: String) -> String
  let at = evolution_last_text_index(&name, "::")
  if at < 0 then name.clone() else name.slice(at + 2, name.len()) end
end

# The type row whose StableDeclId the key parses to (signature changes keep
# the declaration, so an a-side key finds the b-side row).
def evolution_find_type(snapshot: SemanticSnapshot, decl: StableDeclId) -> Option[SemanticType]
  for t in snapshot.types do
    if stable_decl_eq(&stable_decl_of_key(&t.stable_id.key), &decl) then
      return Option::Some(t)
    end
  end
  Option::None
end

# The symbol row whose StableDeclId the key parses to.
def evolution_find_symbol(snapshot: SemanticSnapshot, decl: StableDeclId) -> Option[SemanticSymbol]
  for s in snapshot.symbols do
    if stable_decl_eq(&stable_decl_of_key(&s.stable_id.key), &decl) then
      return Option::Some(s)
    end
  end
  Option::None
end

# Whether a symbol row is a callable def (the signature-plan subject family).
def evolution_symbol_callable(s: SemanticSymbol) -> Bool
  match s.kind
  when DefKind::Function then true
  when DefKind::Method then true
  when _ then false
  end
end

# The persisted ABI surface row of a def key's declaration, by row kind
# word ("fn" | "type"). The typed mirror the plans prefer over text.
def evolution_find_abi_row(
  snapshot: SemanticSnapshot,
  decl: StableDeclId,
  kind_word: String
) -> Option[AbiSurfaceRow]
  for r in snapshot.abi_surfaces do
    if r.kind == kind_word &&
      stable_decl_eq(&stable_decl_of_key(&r.symbol_key), &decl) then
      return Option::Some(r)
    end
  end
  Option::None
end

# The variant names of an enum key's signature render, in declaration
# order. "" for a key whose render is not the enum grammar.
def evolution_enum_variants_of_key(key: String) -> Vec[String]
  let sig = stable_key_signature(&key)
  if !sig.starts_with("enum{") then
    return Vec::new()
  end
  let body = index_brace_body(&sig, 0)
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for part in index_top_level_parts(&body) do
    let name = index_member_name(&part, "(")
    if name.len() > 0 && !out.contains(&name) then
      out.push(name.clone())
    end
  end
  out
end

# The AFTER variant order of one enum type row: the signature render's
# declaration order first (it carries zero-payload variants the typed field
# list omits), then the ABI type row's already-typed variant names that the
# render does not carry (the semantic_index.tg typed-first union mirrored
# as an appendix so the primary order stays declaration order).
def evolution_enum_variant_order(snapshot: SemanticSnapshot, t: SemanticType) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for v in evolution_enum_variants_of_key(&t.stable_id.key) do
    planning_keys_add(&mut out, v)
  end
  let decl = stable_decl_of_key(&t.stable_id.key)
  match evolution_find_abi_row(&snapshot, &decl, "type")
  when Option::Some(r) then
    for v2 in index_abi_member_names(&r.fields, true) do
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, v2)
    end
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  out
end

# The function dependents of a type key: the typed TypeUseEdge users that
# denote functions (a Function / Method symbol row) or carry a MIR summary
# row. Sorted and deduped; the index's type-users accessor IS the typed
# inverse.
def evolution_enum_dependents(
  snapshot: SemanticSnapshot,
  idx: SemanticIndex,
  type_key: String
) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for user in index_type_users_of(&idx, type_key.clone()) do
    if evolution_is_function_key(&snapshot, &idx, &user) then
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, user.clone())
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# Whether a stable key denotes an analyzed function: a recorded MIR summary
# row or a Function / Method symbol row.
def evolution_is_function_key(
  snapshot: SemanticSnapshot,
  idx: SemanticIndex,
  key: String
) -> Bool
  if index_mir_summary_of(&idx, key.clone()).is_some() then
    return true
  end
  let decl = stable_decl_of_key(&key)
  for s in snapshot.symbols do
    if stable_decl_eq(&stable_decl_of_key(&s.stable_id.key), &decl) then
      match s.kind
      when DefKind::Function then return true
      when DefKind::Method then return true
      when _ then ()
      end
    end
  end
  false
end

# The close-paren index of the canonical "fn(...)" signature render (-1
# when the text is not that grammar). Balanced-parser walk — a parameter
# type may itself contain parens / arrows ("fn(fn(Int)->Int)->Unit").
def evolution_sig_close(sig: String) -> Int
  if !sig.starts_with("fn(") then
    return -1
  end
  var depth = 0
  var i = 2
  while i < sig.len() do
    let ch = sig.slice(i, i + 1)
    if ch == "(" then
      depth = depth + 1
    elsif ch == ")" then
      depth = depth - 1
      if depth == 0 then
        return i
      end
    end
    i = i + 1
  end
  -1
end

# The canonical "conv:type" parameter renders of a signature text ([] when
# the text is not the canonical fn grammar; no parameters -> []). Top-level
# commas only (the nesting-aware split).
def evolution_sig_params(sig: String) -> Vec[String]
  let close = evolution_sig_close(&sig)
  if close < 0 || close <= 3 then
    return Vec::new()
  end
  let body = sig.slice(3, close)
  if body.len() == 0 then
    return Vec::new()
  end
  index_top_level_parts(&body)
end

# The canonical return render of a signature text: everything after the
# matched ")->" with the declared-effect suffix ("effects(...)") stripped.
def evolution_sig_return(sig: String) -> String
  let close = evolution_sig_close(&sig)
  if close < 0 then
    return "".to_string()
  end
  let arrow = close + 1
  if arrow + 2 > sig.len() then
    return "".to_string()
  end
  if sig.slice(arrow, arrow + 2) != "->" then
    return "".to_string()
  end
  evolution_strip_effects(&sig.slice(arrow + 2, sig.len()))
end

# Strip a trailing "effects(...)" suffix (the snapshot writer's declared-
# effect id render). The suffix must be balanced to the very end — a return
# type that merely contains the text keeps its full render.
def evolution_strip_effects(s: String) -> String
  let at = evolution_last_text_index(&s, "effects(")
  if at < 0 then
    return s.clone()
  end
  if evolution_parens_balanced(&s.slice(at, s.len())) then
    return s.slice(0, at)
  end
  s.clone()
end

def evolution_parens_balanced(s: String) -> Bool
  var depth = 0
  var i = 0
  while i < s.len() do
    let ch = s.slice(i, i + 1)
    if ch == "(" then
      depth = depth + 1
    elsif ch == ")" then
      depth = depth - 1
      if depth < 0 then
        return false
      end
    end
    i = i + 1
  end
  depth == 0
end

# Split one canonical parameter render "conv:type" at its FIRST ':' (a
# type render never starts with ':').
def evolution_param_parts(token: String) -> (String, String)
  let at = evolution_text_index(&token, ":", 0)
  if at < 0 then
    (token.clone(), "".to_string())
  else
    (token.slice(0, at), token.slice(at + 1, token.len()))
  end
end

# The positional convention changes of one signature evolution.
# TYPED-FIRST: when both sides carry an ABI fn row whose ownership_in lists
# have the same (non-zero) length, that typed list decides; otherwise the
# parsed "conv:type" renders are compared positionally (equal type render,
# different convention word). Rows are "<index>:<old>-><new>", sorted.
def evolution_convention_changes(
  a_abi: Option[AbiSurfaceRow],
  b_abi: Option[AbiSurfaceRow],
  a_params: Vec[String],
  b_params: Vec[String]
) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  match a_abi
  when Option::Some(ar) then
    match b_abi
    when Option::Some(br) then
      if ar.ownership_in.len() == br.ownership_in.len() && ar.ownership_in.len() > 0 then
        var i = 0
        while i < ar.ownership_in.len() do
          if ar.ownership_in[i] != br.ownership_in[i] then
            out.push(i.to_string() + ":" + ar.ownership_in[i].clone() + "->" +
              br.ownership_in[i].clone())
          end
          i = i + 1
        end
        planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
        return out
      end
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  if a_params.len() == b_params.len() then
    var j = 0
    while j < a_params.len() do
      let (a_conv, a_type) = evolution_param_parts(&a_params[j])
      let (b_conv, b_type) = evolution_param_parts(&b_params[j])
      if a_type == b_type && a_conv != b_conv then
        out.push(j.to_string() + ":" + a_conv.clone() + "->" + b_conv.clone())
      end
      j = j + 1
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 3. EnumEvolutionPlan — enum_evolution_plan
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The BEFORE key of an enum's variant set, read from the delta's typed
# carriers in precedence order:
#   1. delta.abi_delta.surface_rows — the per-surface before/after row
#      deltas. The surface id IS "type:<full stable key>", so the before
#      side's key (and therefore its declaration-order variant render) is
#      carried exactly. The a-side and b-side surface ids are DISTINCT
#      (the signature is part of the key), so both entries are scanned.
#   2. delta.public_api_delta.before.rows — the "<digest> type <key>" rows
#      for pub types (the pre-item-18 fallback), matched by declaration.
# Option::None when the delta carries no before side for the declaration:
# the caller then uses the delta's own created/removed variant entity keys
# (see enum_evolution_plan's documented fallback).
def evolution_enum_before_key(delta: SemanticDelta, decl: StableDeclId) -> Option[String]
  for row in delta.abi_delta.surface_rows do
    if row.surface_id.starts_with("type:") then
      let key = row.surface_id.slice(5, row.surface_id.len())
      if stable_decl_eq(&stable_decl_of_key(&key), &decl) then
        match row.before
        when Option::Some(_) then return Option::Some(key)
        when Option::None then ()
        end
      end
    end
  end
  for row2 in delta.public_api_delta.before.rows do
    if row2.contains(" type ") then
      let at = evolution_text_index(&row2, " type ", 0)
      if at >= 0 then
        let key2 = row2.slice(at + 6, row2.len())
        if stable_decl_eq(&stable_decl_of_key(&key2), &decl) then
          return Option::Some(key2)
        end
      end
    end
  end
  Option::None
end

# The variant names a delta's created/removed entity keys attribute to one
# enum declaration: the keys whose signature component is exactly
# "variant" (the snapshot writer's EnumVariant marker) AND whose name-part
# module equals the enum's module. This is the documented CONSERVATIVE
# fallback for a snapshot pair the delta carries no before render for: a
# variant symbol key does not name its owning enum, so the module-scope
# attribution can over-report when two enums share a module (fail-closed
# for planning; the primary abi / api carriers are exact).
def evolution_delta_variant_names(keys: Vec[String], type_key: String) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  let module_key = evolution_name_module(&stable_key_name_part(&type_key))
  for k in keys do
    if stable_key_signature(&k) == "variant" then
      let name_part = stable_key_name_part(&k)
      if evolution_name_module(&name_part) == module_key then
        planning_keys_add(&mut out, evolution_name_last(&name_part))
      end
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# Build the evolution plan of one enum type key against one §31 delta.
# Option::None when the snapshot has no Enum type row for the key's
# declaration. See the module doc for the documented verdict / risk rules
# and the before-set precedence.
pub def enum_evolution_plan(
  snapshot: SemanticSnapshot,
  type_key: String,
  delta: SemanticDelta
) -> Option[EnumEvolutionPlan]
  let decl = stable_decl_of_key(&type_key)
  let b_row = match evolution_find_type(&snapshot, decl.clone())
    when Option::Some(t) then t
    when Option::None then return Option::None
  end
  match b_row.kind
  when SemanticTypeKind::Enum then ()
  when _ then return Option::None
  end
  let b_key = b_row.stable_id.key.clone()
  let b_variants = evolution_enum_variant_order(&snapshot, &b_row)
  var added: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  var removed: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  var reordered = false
  match evolution_enum_before_key(&delta, &decl)
  when Option::Some(a_key) then
    let a_variants = evolution_enum_variants_of_key(&a_key)
    added = evolution_set_minus(&b_variants, &a_variants)
    removed = evolution_set_minus(&a_variants, &b_variants)
    # Reordering is only meaningful when the SET agrees: the order signal
    # is the two declaration-order renders, compared only then (set
    # membership is order-independent; the lists are duplicate-free).
    if added.len() == 0 && removed.len() == 0 then
      reordered = !planning_text_lists_same(&a_variants, &b_variants)
    end
  when Option::None then
    added = evolution_delta_variant_names(delta.created.clone(), b_key.clone())
    removed = evolution_delta_variant_names(delta.removed.clone(), b_key.clone())
  end
  let idx = build_semantic_index(&snapshot)
  let dependents = evolution_enum_dependents(&snapshot, &idx, &b_key)
  var risks: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for v in added do
    planning_keys_add(&mut risks,
      "added-variant:" + v.clone() + ":compatible-unless-exhaustive-match")
  end
  for v2 in removed do
    planning_keys_add(&mut risks, "removed-variant:" + v2.clone() + ":match-may-break")
  end
  if reordered then
    planning_keys_add(&mut risks, "reordered-variants:discriminant-assumptions")
  end
  for d in dependents do
    planning_keys_add(&mut risks, "dependent:" + d.clone())
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut risks)
  let verdict = if removed.len() > 0 || reordered then
    "breaking"
  elsif added.len() > 0 && dependents.len() > 0 then
    "review"
  else
    "compatible"
  end
  Option::Some(EnumEvolutionPlan {
    type_key: b_key,
    added_variants: added,
    removed_variants: removed,
    reordered: reordered,
    risks: risks,
    verdict: verdict
  })
end

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 4. SignatureEvolutionPlan — signature_evolution_plan
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Build the signature evolution plan of one function / method across two
# snapshots. Option::None when neither snapshot declares the key's
# declaration as a callable symbol row. See the module doc for the
# documented verdict rules; parameter identity is the canonical
# "conv:type" render and the ABI fn row is the typed preferred source for
# conventions / return class.
pub def signature_evolution_plan(
  a: SemanticSnapshot,
  b: SemanticSnapshot,
  function_key: String
) -> Option[SignatureEvolutionPlan]
  let decl = stable_decl_of_key(&function_key)
  var a_key = "".to_string()
  var b_key = "".to_string()
  match evolution_find_symbol(&a, decl.clone())
  when Option::Some(s) then
    if !evolution_symbol_callable(&s) then
      return Option::None
    end
    a_key = s.stable_id.key.clone()
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  match evolution_find_symbol(&b, decl.clone())
  when Option::Some(s2) then
    if !evolution_symbol_callable(&s2) then
      return Option::None
    end
    b_key = s2.stable_id.key.clone()
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  if a_key.len() == 0 && b_key.len() == 0 then
    return Option::None
  end
  let a_sig = if a_key.len() > 0 then stable_key_signature(&a_key) else "".to_string() end
  let b_sig = if b_key.len() > 0 then stable_key_signature(&b_key) else "".to_string() end
  let a_params = evolution_sig_params(&a_sig)
  let b_params = evolution_sig_params(&b_sig)
  let param_added = evolution_multiset_minus(b_params.clone(), a_params.clone())
  let param_removed = evolution_multiset_minus(a_params.clone(), b_params.clone())
  let param_reordered = param_added.len() == 0 && param_removed.len() == 0 &&
    a_params.len() == b_params.len() && !planning_text_lists_same(&a_params, &b_params)
  let a_ret = evolution_sig_return(&a_sig)
  let b_ret = evolution_sig_return(&b_sig)
  let a_abi = evolution_find_abi_row(&a, &decl, "fn")
  let b_abi = evolution_find_abi_row(&b, &decl, "fn")
  var return_changed = a_ret != b_ret
  match a_abi
  when Option::Some(ar) then
    match b_abi
    when Option::Some(br) then
      if ar.ret_class != br.ret_class then
        return_changed = true
      end
    when Option::None then ()
    end
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  let convention_changes = evolution_convention_changes(&a_abi, &b_abi, &a_params, &b_params)
  let function_text = if b_key.len() > 0 then b_key.clone() else a_key.clone() end
  let idx = if b_key.len() > 0 then build_semantic_index(&b) else build_semantic_index(&a) end
  let callers = index_callers_of(&idx, function_text.clone())
  let unchanged = a_sig == b_sig && !return_changed &&
    convention_changes.len() == 0 && planning_text_lists_same(&a_params, &b_params)
  var verdict = "".to_string()
  if unchanged then
    verdict = "compatible"
  elsif param_added.len() > 0 || param_removed.len() > 0 || param_reordered ||
    return_changed || convention_changes.len() > 0 then
    verdict = "breaking"
  else
    # The canonical text changed in a dimension this plan does not
    # classify (today: the declared-effect id suffix).
    verdict = "review"
  end
  Option::Some(SignatureEvolutionPlan {
    function: function_text,
    param_added: param_added,
    param_removed: param_removed,
    param_reordered: param_reordered,
    return_changed: return_changed,
    convention_changes: convention_changes,
    callers: callers,
    verdict: verdict
  })
end

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 5. TraitEvolutionPlan — trait_evolution_plan
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The declared method names of a trait key's "trait{...}" signature render,
# sorted and deduped (the trait's declared properties).
def evolution_trait_methods_of_key(key: String) -> Vec[String]
  if key.len() == 0 then
    return Vec::new()
  end
  let sig = stable_key_signature(&key)
  if !sig.starts_with("trait{") then
    return Vec::new()
  end
  let body = index_brace_body(&sig, 0)
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for part in index_top_level_parts(&body) do
    let name = index_member_name(&part, "(")
    if name.len() > 0 then
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, name)
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# The typed impl rows of a trait declaration: the TraitImplEdge inverse
# renders "self-type|impl-key", sorted and deduped.
def evolution_trait_impl_rows(
  snapshot: SemanticSnapshot,
  trait_decl: StableDeclId
) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for e in snapshot.dependencies.trait_impls do
    if stable_decl_eq(&stable_decl_of_key(&e.trait_key), &trait_decl) then
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, e.self_type.clone() + "|" + e.impl_key.clone())
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# The selected impl-method def keys of one impl key (the TraitSelectionEdge
# inverse), sorted and deduped.
def evolution_trait_impl_selected(snapshot: SemanticSnapshot, impl_key: String) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for e in snapshot.dependencies.trait_selections do
    if e.impl_key == impl_key then
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, e.function.clone())
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# Whether one selected impl-method def key covers a trait method name: the
# key's name-part IS the method name or ends with "::<method>".
def evolution_method_covered(selected_key: String, method: String) -> Bool
  let name = stable_key_name_part(&selected_key)
  if name == method then
    return true
  end
  let suffix = "::" + method.clone()
  name.ends_with(&suffix)
end

# Build the trait evolution plan of one trait key across two snapshots.
# Option::None when neither snapshot declares the key's declaration as a
# Trait type row. See the module doc for the documented verdict rules; the
# impl rows / selections come from the side that carries the trait row
# (the b side when it exists).
pub def trait_evolution_plan(
  a: SemanticSnapshot,
  b: SemanticSnapshot,
  trait_key: String
) -> Option[TraitEvolutionPlan]
  let decl = stable_decl_of_key(&trait_key)
  var a_key = "".to_string()
  var b_key = "".to_string()
  match evolution_find_type(&a, decl.clone())
  when Option::Some(t) then
    match t.kind
    when SemanticTypeKind::Trait then a_key = t.stable_id.key.clone()
    when _ then return Option::None
    end
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  match evolution_find_type(&b, decl.clone())
  when Option::Some(t2) then
    match t2.kind
    when SemanticTypeKind::Trait then b_key = t2.stable_id.key.clone()
    when _ then return Option::None
    end
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  if a_key.len() == 0 && b_key.len() == 0 then
    return Option::None
  end
  let a_methods = evolution_trait_methods_of_key(&a_key)
  let b_methods = evolution_trait_methods_of_key(&b_key)
  let methods_added = evolution_set_minus(&b_methods, &a_methods)
  let methods_removed = evolution_set_minus(&a_methods, &b_methods)
  var impl_rows: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  if b_key.len() > 0 then
    impl_rows = evolution_trait_impl_rows(&b, &decl)
  else
    impl_rows = evolution_trait_impl_rows(&a, &decl)
  end
  var risky: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for row in impl_rows do
    let impl_key = evolution_text_after_first(&row, "|")
    var selected: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
    if b_key.len() > 0 then
      selected = evolution_trait_impl_selected(&b, impl_key.clone())
    else
      selected = evolution_trait_impl_selected(&a, impl_key.clone())
    end
    var missing = false
    for m in methods_added do
      var covered = false
      for fn_key in selected do
        if evolution_method_covered(&fn_key, &m) then
          covered = true
        end
      end
      if !covered then
        missing = true
      end
    end
    if missing then
      planning_keys_add(&mut risky, row.clone())
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut impl_rows)
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut risky)
  let verdict = if risky.len() > 0 then
    "breaking"
  elsif methods_added.len() > 0 || methods_removed.len() > 0 then
    "review"
  else
    "compatible"
  end
  let trait_text = if b_key.len() > 0 then b_key.clone() else a_key.clone() end
  Option::Some(TraitEvolutionPlan {
    trait_key: trait_text,
    methods_added: methods_added,
    methods_removed: methods_removed,
    impls: impl_rows,
    risky_impls: risky,
    verdict: verdict
  })
end

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 6. CapabilityPropagationPlan — capability_propagation_plan
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The changed capability / effect row keys of one delta (the plan's
# `changed` derivation):
#   - each effect row newly carrying a §11 class contributes its function
#     key (once, regardless of how many classes were added);
#   - each capability id an effect row's after view newly carries
#     contributes the normalized "fn|cap<id>" key;
#   - each capability edge that toggled Absent -> Present contributes its
#     "fn|cap<id>" row key.
# Sorted and deduped.
def evolution_capability_changed(delta: SemanticDelta) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for row in delta.effect_delta do
    var has_class = false
    for bit in planning_class_bits() do
      if planning_effect_added_class(&row, bit) then
        has_class = true
      end
    end
    if has_class then
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, row.function.clone())
    end
    for id_text in row.after.capabilities do
      if planning_effect_added_cap(&row, id_text.clone()) then
        planning_keys_add(&mut out,
          row.function.clone() + "|" + planning_capability_text(id_text.clone()))
      end
    end
  end
  for row2 in delta.capability_delta do
    match row2.before
    when Presence::Present then ()
    when Presence::Absent then
      match row2.after
      when Presence::Absent then ()
      when Presence::Present then
        planning_keys_add(&mut out, row2.function.clone() + "|" + row2.capability.clone())
      end
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# The Unknown indirect-call SITES recorded for one caller (the §29
# IndirectCallEdge rows with completeness "Unknown"), sorted and deduped.
def evolution_unknown_indirect_sites(snapshot: SemanticSnapshot, caller: String) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for ic in snapshot.indirect_calls do
    if ic.caller == caller && ic.completeness == "Unknown" then
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, ic.site.clone())
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# Whether a caller key is OUTSIDE the analyzed program: no symbol row and
# no MIR summary row records its declaration in the snapshot.
def evolution_node_external(snapshot: SemanticSnapshot, idx: SemanticIndex, key: String) -> Bool
  if index_symbol_get(&idx, key.clone()).is_some() then
    return false
  end
  if index_mir_summary_of(&idx, key.clone()).is_some() then
    return false
  end
  true
end

# Build the capability propagation plan of one delta over one snapshot's
# call graph (the after / current snapshot — the call rows are read from
# it). See the module doc for the documented walk / verdict rules.
pub def capability_propagation_plan(
  snapshot: SemanticSnapshot,
  delta: SemanticDelta
) -> CapabilityPropagationPlan
  let changed = evolution_capability_changed(&delta)
  var roots: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for k in changed do
    planning_keys_add(&mut roots, planning_key_root(&k))
  end
  let idx = build_semantic_index(&snapshot)
  var seen: Map[String, Bool] = Map::new()
  var queue: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for r in roots do
    if !seen.contains_key(&r) then
      seen.insert(r.clone(), true)
      queue.push(r.clone())
    end
  end
  var propagated: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  var blocked: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  var head = 0
  while head < queue.len() do
    let node = queue[head].clone()
    head = head + 1
    let unknown_sites = evolution_unknown_indirect_sites(&snapshot, node.clone())
    if unknown_sites.len() > 0 then
      # The function makes at least one call with an unknown callee: the
      # effect set beyond it is not enumerable, so the walk stops here
      # (fail-closed) and the site rows are the blocked frontier.
      for site in unknown_sites do
        planning_keys_add(&mut blocked, node.clone() + "|unknown-indirect:" + site.clone())
      end
    else
      for caller in index_callers_of(&idx, node.clone()) do
        if !seen.contains_key(&caller) then
          seen.insert(caller.clone(), true)
          planning_keys_add(&mut propagated, caller.clone())
          if evolution_node_external(&snapshot, &idx, caller.clone()) then
            planning_keys_add(&mut blocked, caller.clone() + "|external")
          else
            queue.push(caller.clone())
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut propagated)
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut blocked)
  let verdict = if changed.len() > 0 then "review" else "compatible" end
  CapabilityPropagationPlan {
    changed: changed,
    propagated_to: propagated,
    blocked_at: blocked,
    verdict: verdict
  }
end

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 7. THE §36 BUDGET MAPPING
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE ALLOWANCE-ROW GRAMMAR (the mapping's documented contract):
#   allowed_symbols:<stable key>
#     -> ChangeBudget.allowed_symbols: insert stable_decl_of_key(<key>)
#        (declaration-grain; covers created / removed / modified / affected).
#   allowed_public_api_changes:<stable key>
#     -> ChangeBudget.allowed_public_api_changes (the exact key the
#        budget_public_api_row_key parse yields).
#   allowed_abi_changes:<stable key>
#     -> ChangeBudget.allowed_abi_changes (the exact "symbol=" key).
#   allowed_effect_additions:<fn key>
#     -> ChangeBudget.allowed_effect_additions (the effect row's function
#        key — budget_verify check 5's exact membership).
#   allowed_capability_additions:<fn key>|cap<id>
#     -> ChangeBudget.allowed_capability_additions (budget_verify check 6's
#        exact "fn|cap<id>" key).
# A plan's items contribute the declaration-grain rows; supplying the delta
# adds the EXACT row-key grain (every public-api / abi symmetric-difference
# row's key, every effect / capability addition key, and the allowed_symbols
# declarations of created / removed / modified / affected keys), so a
# budget built from the returned rows admits the delta by construction.
# Unused allowance rows are inert in budget_verify.

# The per-plan mapping: every change ITEM the plan names contributes its
# documented allowance rows (a breaking plan's items are all mapped; a
# review-only item is mapped too, because budget_verify rejects the delta's
# rows whatever the plan's verdict says).
pub def evolution_plan_to_budget_constraints(plan: EvolutionPlan) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  match plan
  when EvolutionPlan::EnumPlan(p) then
    if p.added_variants.len() > 0 || p.removed_variants.len() > 0 || p.reordered then
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_symbols:" + p.type_key.clone())
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_public_api_changes:" + p.type_key.clone())
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_abi_changes:" + p.type_key.clone())
    end
  when EvolutionPlan::SignaturePlan(p) then
    if p.verdict != "compatible" then
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_symbols:" + p.function.clone())
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_public_api_changes:" + p.function.clone())
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_abi_changes:" + p.function.clone())
    end
  when EvolutionPlan::TraitPlan(p) then
    if p.verdict != "compatible" then
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_symbols:" + p.trait_key.clone())
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_public_api_changes:" + p.trait_key.clone())
    end
    for risky in p.risky_impls do
      # The obligation site: the impl's self type (the row is
      # "self-type|impl-key" — the self type is the stable declaration the
      # impl methods register under).
      let self_type = evolution_text_before_first(&risky, "|")
      if self_type.len() > 0 then
        planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_symbols:" + self_type)
      end
    end
  when EvolutionPlan::CapabilityPlan(p) then
    for item in p.changed do
      let root = planning_key_root(&item)
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_symbols:" + root.clone())
      if item.contains("|") then
        planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_capability_additions:" + item.clone())
      else
        planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_effect_additions:" + item.clone())
      end
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# The exact delta-row allowance rows of ONE §31 delta (the delta-refined
# grain of the mapping; see the section doc).
pub def evolution_budget_constraints_of_delta(delta: SemanticDelta) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for k in delta.created do
    planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_symbols:" + k.clone())
  end
  for k2 in delta.removed do
    planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_symbols:" + k2.clone())
  end
  for e in delta.modified do
    planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_symbols:" + e.stable_id.clone())
  end
  for k3 in delta.affected do
    planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_symbols:" + k3.clone())
  end
  for row in semantic_delta_rows_diff(&delta.public_api_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.public_api_delta.after.rows) do
    planning_keys_add(&mut out,
      "allowed_public_api_changes:" + budget_public_api_row_key(&row))
  end
  for row2 in semantic_delta_rows_diff(&delta.abi_delta.before.rows,
    &delta.abi_delta.after.rows) do
    planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_abi_changes:" + budget_abi_row_key(&row2))
  end
  for row3 in delta.effect_delta do
    var has_class = false
    for bit in planning_class_bits() do
      if planning_effect_added_class(&row3, bit) then
        has_class = true
      end
    end
    if has_class then
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, "allowed_effect_additions:" + row3.function.clone())
    end
    for id_text in row3.after.capabilities do
      if planning_effect_added_cap(&row3, id_text.clone()) then
        let cap_id = budget_effect_cap_id_of(id_text.clone())
        if cap_id >= 0 then
          planning_keys_add(&mut out,
            "allowed_capability_additions:" +
            budget_capability_addition_key(row3.function.clone(), cap_id))
        end
      end
    end
  end
  for row4 in delta.capability_delta do
    match row4.before
    when Presence::Present then ()
    when Presence::Absent then
      match row4.after
      when Presence::Absent then ()
      when Presence::Present then
        let cap_id2 = budget_cap_id_of(row4.capability.clone())
        if cap_id2 >= 0 then
          planning_keys_add(&mut out,
            "allowed_capability_additions:" +
            budget_capability_addition_key(row4.function.clone(), cap_id2))
        end
      end
    end
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# The FAMILY mapping: every plan's allowance rows, plus (when a delta is
# supplied) the exact delta-row grain, sorted and deduped. This is the
# function a task calls to obtain the constraint rows it writes into its
# §36 ChangeBudget.
pub def evolution_plans_to_budget_constraints(
  plans: Vec[EvolutionPlan],
  delta: Option[SemanticDelta] = Option::None
) -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for p in plans do
    for r in evolution_plan_to_budget_constraints(p) do
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, r)
    end
  end
  match delta
  when Option::Some(d) then
    for r2 in evolution_budget_constraints_of_delta(d) do
      planning_keys_add(&mut out, r2)
    end
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  planning_sorted_keys(&mut out)
  out
end

# The INVERSE mapping: build a §36 ChangeBudget from the allowance rows
# (the documented grammar above). Rows outside the grammar are ignored
# (fail-open on unknown text is avoided because every emitted row is one
# of the five documented families; the caller's row set is its own).
pub def evolution_budget_of_constraints(constraints: Vec[String]) -> ChangeBudget
  var syms: Set[StableDeclId] = Set::new()
  var api: Set[String] = Set::new()
  var abi: Set[String] = Set::new()
  var effects: Set[String] = Set::new()
  var caps: Set[String] = Set::new()
  for row in constraints do
    if row.starts_with("allowed_symbols:") then
      let p1 = "allowed_symbols:"
      syms.insert(stable_decl_of_key(&row.slice(p1.len(), row.len())))
    elsif row.starts_with("allowed_public_api_changes:") then
      let p2 = "allowed_public_api_changes:"
      api.insert(row.slice(p2.len(), row.len()))
    elsif row.starts_with("allowed_abi_changes:") then
      let p3 = "allowed_abi_changes:"
      abi.insert(row.slice(p3.len(), row.len()))
    elsif row.starts_with("allowed_effect_additions:") then
      let p4 = "allowed_effect_additions:"
      effects.insert(row.slice(p4.len(), row.len()))
    elsif row.starts_with("allowed_capability_additions:") then
      let p5 = "allowed_capability_additions:"
      caps.insert(row.slice(p5.len(), row.len()))
    end
  end
  ChangeBudget {
    allowed_symbols: syms,
    allowed_public_api_changes: api,
    allowed_abi_changes: abi,
    allowed_effect_additions: effects,
    allowed_capability_additions: caps
  }
end

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 8. THE EXECUTABLE LANE ROWS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The sibling style of semantic_planning.tg's lane: the rows build small
# snapshot pairs through the semantic_delta.tg lane fixtures, diff them
# through the REAL semantic_delta_of, run the plan builders and compare
# the answers / constraint rows against the documented expectations. Each
# sub-lane returns the mismatch rows (empty = the lane verifies); the
# aggregate semantic_evolution_lane_check runs them all.
#
#   EN — enum plans: E1 addition with a dependent (review), E2 removal
#        (breaking), E3 reorder (breaking), E4 no change (compatible),
#        E5 non-enum -> None, E6 addition without dependents (compatible),
#        E7 the public-api before-row fallback, E8 the delta-entity-key
#        fallback.
#   SG — signature plans: S1 unchanged (compatible), S2 added parameter
#        (breaking, no-default rule), S3 removed parameter, S4 reorder,
#        S5 return change, S6 parsed convention change, S7 declared-effect
#        suffix change (review), S8 typed ABI ownership_in preference, S9
#        typed ABI ret_class signal, S10 unknown function -> None.
#   TR — trait plans: T1 added method + impl lacking it (breaking), T2
#        added method covered by the selection (review), T3 removed method
#        (review), T4 no change (compatible), T5 non-trait -> None.
#   CP — capability propagation: C1 the transitive walk with an external
#        caller and an unknown-indirect frontier, C2 the empty delta.
#   BD — the budget mapping: the exact constraint rows per plan family,
#        the fail-closed empty budget, and the end-to-end round trip (the
#        delta-refined rows -> ChangeBudget -> budget_verify []).

def evolution_lane_bool(inout out: Vec[String], name: String, ok: Bool) -> Unit
  if !ok then
    out.push(name + ": assertion failed")
  end
  ()
end

def evolution_lane_text(inout out: Vec[String], name: String, got: String, expected: String) -> Unit
  if got != expected then
    out.push(name + ": expected " + expected + ", got " + got)
  end
  ()
end

def evolution_lane_keys(inout out: Vec[String], name: String, got: Vec[String], expected: Vec[String]) -> Unit
  if !planning_text_lists_same(&got, &expected) then
    out.push(name + ": expected [" + expected.join(",") + "], got [" + got.join(",") + "]")
  end
  ()
end

# The hand-built ABI type row of an enum key: the typed field list in
# declaration order (the tag row plus one "Variant#0 offset size" row per
# payload variant) — the abi_surfaces "type" row the plan's typed variant
# source reads.
def evolution_lane_abi_type_row(key: String, variants: Vec[String]) -> AbiSurfaceRow
  var fields: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  fields.push("tag 0 1")
  var off = 1
  for v in variants do
    fields.push(v.clone() + "#0 " + off.to_string() + " 4")
    off = off + 4
  end
  AbiSurfaceRow {
    surface_id: "type:" + key.clone(),
    symbol_key: key.clone(),
    kind: "type",
    size: off,
    alignment: 4,
    fields: fields
  }
end

# The hand-built ABI fn row: the typed convention mirror (ownership_in /
# param_classes) plus the return class.
def evolution_lane_abi_fn_row(
  key: String,
  conventions: Vec[String],
  ret_class: String
) -> AbiSurfaceRow
  AbiSurfaceRow {
    surface_id: "fn:" + key.clone(),
    symbol_key: key.clone(),
    kind: "fn",
    size: -1,
    alignment: -1,
    arg_classes: conventions.clone(),
    param_classes: conventions.clone(),
    ownership_in: conventions,
    ret_class: ret_class,
    calling_convention: "tangerine".to_string(),
    ownership_out: "owned".to_string(),
    failure_convention: "trap".to_string(),
    platform: "lane".to_string()
  }
end

# One enum snapshot side.
def evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(
  key: String,
  variants: Vec[String],
  type_pub: Bool,
  with_abi: Bool,
  with_dependent: Bool,
  with_variant_symbols: Bool
) -> SemanticSnapshot
  var s = delta_lane_snapshot()
  var types: Vec[SemanticType] = Vec::new()
  types.push(delta_lane_type_row(&key, "E", SemanticTypeKind::Enum, type_pub))
  s.types = types
  if with_abi then
    var abi: Vec[AbiSurfaceRow] = Vec::new()
    abi.push(evolution_lane_abi_type_row(&key, variants.clone()))
    s.abi_surfaces = abi
  end
  var syms: Vec[SemanticSymbol] = Vec::new()
  if with_dependent then
    syms.push(delta_lane_fn_symbol("m::use_e#fn()->unit", "use_e", false))
  end
  if with_variant_symbols then
    for v in variants do
      syms.push(SemanticSymbol {
        stable_id: delta_lane_sid(&("m::" + v.clone() + "#variant")),
        kind: DefKind::EnumVariant,
        name: v.clone(),
        module_path: "m".to_string(),
        is_pub: true,
        is_generic: false
      })
    end
  end
  s.symbols = syms
  if with_dependent then
    s.dependencies = SemanticDependencyGraph {
      type_uses: Vec::from([
        TypeUseEdge {
          user: "m::use_e#fn()->unit".to_string(),
          used_type: key.clone()
        }
      ])
    }
  end
  s
end

def evolution_lane_enum_check() -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()

  # ———— E1: A,B -> A,B,C with a dependent function (review) ————
  let e1_key = "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int),C(int)}".to_string()
  let a1 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(
    "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int)}".to_string(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string()]), true, true, true, false)
  let b1 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(e1_key.clone(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string(), "C".to_string()]), true, true, true, false)
  let d1 = semantic_delta_of(&a1, &b1)
  match enum_evolution_plan(&b1, e1_key.clone(), d1)
  when Option::Some(p) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "E1-verdict", p.verdict.clone(), "review")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "E1-added", p.added_variants.clone(), Vec::from([
      "C".to_string()
    ]))
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "E1-removed", p.removed_variants.clone(), Vec::new())
    evolution_lane_bool(&mut out, "E1-reordered", !p.reordered)
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "E1-risks", p.risks.clone(), Vec::from([
      "added-variant:C:compatible-unless-exhaustive-match".to_string(),
      "dependent:m::use_e#fn()->unit".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("E1: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— E2: A,B,C -> A,B (breaking removal) ————
  let e2_key = "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int)}".to_string()
  let a2 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(
    "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int),C(int)}".to_string(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string(), "C".to_string()]), true, true, true, false)
  let b2 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(e2_key.clone(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string()]), true, true, true, false)
  let d2 = semantic_delta_of(&a2, &b2)
  match enum_evolution_plan(&b2, e2_key.clone(), d2)
  when Option::Some(p2) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "E2-verdict", p2.verdict.clone(), "breaking")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "E2-removed", p2.removed_variants.clone(), Vec::from([
      "C".to_string()
    ]))
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "E2-risks", p2.risks.clone(), Vec::from([
      "dependent:m::use_e#fn()->unit".to_string(),
      "removed-variant:C:match-may-break".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("E2: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— E3: A,B -> B,A (breaking reorder) ————
  let e3_key = "m::E#enum{B(int),A(int)}".to_string()
  let a3 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(
    "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int)}".to_string(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string()]), true, true, true, false)
  let b3 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(e3_key.clone(),
    Vec::from(["B".to_string(), "A".to_string()]), true, true, true, false)
  let d3 = semantic_delta_of(&a3, &b3)
  match enum_evolution_plan(&b3, e3_key.clone(), d3)
  when Option::Some(p3) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "E3-verdict", p3.verdict.clone(), "breaking")
    evolution_lane_bool(&mut out, "E3-reordered", p3.reordered)
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "E3-added", p3.added_variants.clone(), Vec::new())
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "E3-risks", p3.risks.clone(), Vec::from([
      "dependent:m::use_e#fn()->unit".to_string(),
      "reordered-variants:discriminant-assumptions".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("E3: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— E4: no change (compatible) ————
  let e4_key = "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int)}".to_string()
  let a4 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(e4_key.clone(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string()]), true, true, true, false)
  let b4 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(e4_key.clone(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string()]), true, true, true, false)
  let d4 = semantic_delta_of(&a4, &b4)
  match enum_evolution_plan(&b4, e4_key.clone(), d4)
  when Option::Some(p4) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "E4-verdict", p4.verdict.clone(), "compatible")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "E4-risks", p4.risks.clone(), Vec::new())
    evolution_lane_bool(&mut out, "E4-reordered", !p4.reordered)
  when Option::None then
    out.push("E4: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— E5: a non-enum key -> None ————
  var s5 = delta_lane_snapshot()
  var t5: Vec[SemanticType] = Vec::new()
  t5.push(delta_lane_type_row("m::S#struct{x:int}".to_string(), "S",
    SemanticTypeKind::Struct, false))
  s5.types = t5
  match enum_evolution_plan(&s5, "m::S#struct{x:int}".to_string(), semantic_delta_empty())
  when Option::Some(_) then
    out.push("E5: expected Option::None")
  when Option::None then ()
  end

  # ———— E6: A -> A,B without dependents (compatible) ————
  let e6_key = "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int)}".to_string()
  let a6 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(
    "m::E#enum{A(int)}".to_string(), Vec::from(["A".to_string()]), true, true, false, false)
  let b6 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(e6_key.clone(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string()]), true, true, false, false)
  let d6 = semantic_delta_of(&a6, &b6)
  match enum_evolution_plan(&b6, e6_key.clone(), d6)
  when Option::Some(p6) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "E6-verdict", p6.verdict.clone(), "compatible")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "E6-risks", p6.risks.clone(), Vec::from([
      "added-variant:B:compatible-unless-exhaustive-match".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("E6: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— E7: the public-api before-row fallback (no abi_surfaces rows) ————
  let e7_key = "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int),C(int)}".to_string()
  let a7 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(
    "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int)}".to_string(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string()]), true, false, true, false)
  let b7 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(e7_key.clone(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string(), "C".to_string()]), true, false, true, false)
  let d7 = semantic_delta_of(&a7, &b7)
  match enum_evolution_plan(&b7, e7_key.clone(), d7)
  when Option::Some(p7) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "E7-verdict", p7.verdict.clone(), "review")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "E7-added", p7.added_variants.clone(), Vec::from([
      "C".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("E7: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— E8: the delta-entity-key fallback (non-pub, no abi rows) ————
  let e8_key = "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int)}".to_string()
  let a8 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(
    "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int),C(int)}".to_string(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string(), "C".to_string()]), false, false, false, true)
  let b8 = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(e8_key.clone(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string()]), false, false, false, true)
  let d8 = semantic_delta_of(&a8, &b8)
  match enum_evolution_plan(&b8, e8_key.clone(), d8)
  when Option::Some(p8) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "E8-verdict", p8.verdict.clone(), "breaking")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "E8-removed", p8.removed_variants.clone(), Vec::from([
      "C".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("E8: expected a plan")
  end

  out
end

# One signature snapshot side (the fn symbol plus a caller row on the b
# side when requested).
def evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(key: String, with_caller: Bool) -> SemanticSnapshot
  var s = delta_lane_snapshot()
  var syms: Vec[SemanticSymbol] = Vec::new()
  syms.push(delta_lane_fn_symbol(&key, "f", true))
  if with_caller then
    syms.push(delta_lane_fn_symbol("m::caller#fn()->unit", "caller", false))
  end
  s.symbols = syms
  if with_caller then
    var calls: Vec[CallEdge] = Vec::new()
    calls.push(CallEdge {
      caller: delta_lane_sid("m::caller#fn()->unit"),
      callee: delta_lane_sid(&key),
      kind: CallEdgeKind::Direct
    })
    s.calls = calls
  end
  s
end

def evolution_lane_signature_check() -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()

  # ———— S1: unchanged (compatible; callers still reported) ————
  let s1_key = "m::f#fn(let:Int)->Int".to_string()
  let a1 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s1_key.clone(), false)
  let b1 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s1_key.clone(), true)
  match signature_evolution_plan(&a1, &b1, s1_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p1) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "S1-verdict", p1.verdict.clone(), "compatible")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "S1-callers", p1.callers.clone(), Vec::from([
      "m::caller#fn()->unit".to_string()
    ]))
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "S1-added", p1.param_added.clone(), Vec::new())
  when Option::None then
    out.push("S1: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— S2: an added parameter (breaking — no-default rule) ————
  let s2_key = "m::f#fn(let:Int,let:Bool)->Int".to_string()
  let a2 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot("m::f#fn(let:Int)->Int".to_string(), false)
  let b2 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s2_key.clone(), true)
  match signature_evolution_plan(&a2, &b2, s2_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p2) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "S2-verdict", p2.verdict.clone(), "breaking")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "S2-added", p2.param_added.clone(), Vec::from([
      "let:Bool".to_string()
    ]))
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "S2-callers", p2.callers.clone(), Vec::from([
      "m::caller#fn()->unit".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("S2: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— S3: a removed parameter ————
  let s3_key = "m::f#fn(let:Bool)->Int".to_string()
  let a3 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot("m::f#fn(let:Int)->Int".to_string(), false)
  let b3 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s3_key.clone(), true)
  match signature_evolution_plan(&a3, &b3, s3_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p3) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "S3-verdict", p3.verdict.clone(), "breaking")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "S3-removed", p3.param_removed.clone(), Vec::from([
      "let:Int".to_string()
    ]))
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "S3-added", p3.param_added.clone(), Vec::from([
      "let:Bool".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("S3: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— S4: a parameter reorder (same multiset, different order) ————
  let s4_key = "m::f#fn(let:Bool,let:Int)->Int".to_string()
  let a4 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot("m::f#fn(let:Int,let:Bool)->Int".to_string(), false)
  let b4 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s4_key.clone(), true)
  match signature_evolution_plan(&a4, &b4, s4_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p4) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "S4-verdict", p4.verdict.clone(), "breaking")
    evolution_lane_bool(&mut out, "S4-reordered", p4.param_reordered)
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "S4-added", p4.param_added.clone(), Vec::new())
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "S4-removed", p4.param_removed.clone(), Vec::new())
  when Option::None then
    out.push("S4: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— S5: a return change ————
  let s5_key = "m::f#fn(let:Int)->Bool".to_string()
  let a5 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot("m::f#fn(let:Int)->Int".to_string(), false)
  let b5 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s5_key.clone(), true)
  match signature_evolution_plan(&a5, &b5, s5_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p5) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "S5-verdict", p5.verdict.clone(), "breaking")
    evolution_lane_bool(&mut out, "S5-return", p5.return_changed)
  when Option::None then
    out.push("S5: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— S6: a parsed convention change ————
  let s6_key = "m::f#fn(inout:Int)->Int".to_string()
  let a6 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot("m::f#fn(let:Int)->Int".to_string(), false)
  let b6 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s6_key.clone(), true)
  match signature_evolution_plan(&a6, &b6, s6_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p6) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "S6-verdict", p6.verdict.clone(), "breaking")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "S6-conventions", p6.convention_changes.clone(), Vec::from([
      "0:let->inout".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("S6: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— S7: a declared-effect suffix change (review) ————
  let s7_key = "m::f#fn(let:Int)->Inteffects(e1)".to_string()
  let a7 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot("m::f#fn(let:Int)->Int".to_string(), false)
  let b7 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s7_key.clone(), true)
  match signature_evolution_plan(&a7, &b7, s7_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p7) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "S7-verdict", p7.verdict.clone(), "review")
    evolution_lane_bool(&mut out, "S7-return", !p7.return_changed)
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "S7-conventions", p7.convention_changes.clone(), Vec::new())
  when Option::None then
    out.push("S7: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— S8: the typed ABI ownership_in mirror decides conventions ————
  let s8_key = "m::f#fn(let:Int)->Int".to_string()
  var a8 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s8_key.clone(), false)
  a8.abi_surfaces = Vec::from([
    evolution_lane_abi_fn_row(&s8_key,
      Vec::from(["let".to_string()]), "direct:scalar:8".to_string())
  ])
  var b8 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s8_key.clone(), true)
  b8.abi_surfaces = Vec::from([
    evolution_lane_abi_fn_row(&s8_key,
      Vec::from(["inout".to_string()]), "direct:scalar:8".to_string())
  ])
  match signature_evolution_plan(&a8, &b8, s8_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p8) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "S8-verdict", p8.verdict.clone(), "breaking")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "S8-conventions", p8.convention_changes.clone(), Vec::from([
      "0:let->inout".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("S8: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— S9: the typed ABI ret_class signal ————
  let s9_key = "m::f#fn(let:Int)->Int".to_string()
  var a9 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s9_key.clone(), false)
  a9.abi_surfaces = Vec::from([
    evolution_lane_abi_fn_row(&s9_key,
      Vec::from(["let".to_string()]), "direct:scalar:8".to_string())
  ])
  var b9 = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s9_key.clone(), true)
  b9.abi_surfaces = Vec::from([
    evolution_lane_abi_fn_row(&s9_key,
      Vec::from(["let".to_string()]), "sret:by-address:16".to_string())
  ])
  match signature_evolution_plan(&a9, &b9, s9_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p9) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "S9-verdict", p9.verdict.clone(), "breaking")
    evolution_lane_bool(&mut out, "S9-return", p9.return_changed)
  when Option::None then
    out.push("S9: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— S10: an unknown function key -> None ————
  match signature_evolution_plan(&a1, &b1, "m::missing#fn()->unit".to_string())
  when Option::Some(_) then
    out.push("S10: expected Option::None")
  when Option::None then ()
  end

  out
end

def evolution_lane_trait_snapshot(
  key: String,
  with_impl: Bool,
  with_selection_step: Bool
) -> SemanticSnapshot
  var s = delta_lane_snapshot()
  var types: Vec[SemanticType] = Vec::new()
  types.push(delta_lane_type_row(&key, "Tr", SemanticTypeKind::Trait, true))
  s.types = types
  if with_impl then
    let impl_key = "impl::m::S#struct{}|as|" + key.clone()
    var selections: Vec[TraitSelectionEdge] = Vec::new()
    selections.push(TraitSelectionEdge {
      function: "m::S::run#fn(let:Int)->Unit".to_string(),
      trait_key: key.clone(),
      impl_key: impl_key.clone()
    })
    if with_selection_step then
      selections.push(TraitSelectionEdge {
        function: "m::S::step#fn(let:Int)->Unit".to_string(),
        trait_key: key.clone(),
        impl_key: impl_key.clone()
      })
    end
    s.dependencies = SemanticDependencyGraph {
      trait_impls: Vec::from([
        TraitImplEdge {
          impl_key: impl_key,
          trait_key: key.clone(),
          self_type: "m::S#struct{}".to_string()
        }
      ]),
      trait_selections: selections
    }
  end
  s
end

def evolution_lane_trait_impl_row(key: String) -> String
  "m::S#struct{}|impl::m::S#struct{}|as|" + key.clone()
end

def evolution_lane_trait_check() -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()

  # ———— T1: run -> run,step with an impl selecting only run (breaking) ————
  let t1_key = "m::Tr#trait{run(let:Int)->Unit,step(let:Int)->Unit}".to_string()
  let a1 = evolution_lane_trait_snapshot(
    "m::Tr#trait{run(let:Int)->Unit}".to_string(), true, true)
  let b1 = evolution_lane_trait_snapshot(t1_key.clone(), true, false)
  match trait_evolution_plan(&a1, &b1, t1_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p1) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "T1-verdict", p1.verdict.clone(), "breaking")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "T1-added", p1.methods_added.clone(), Vec::from([
      "step".to_string()
    ]))
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "T1-impls", p1.impls.clone(), Vec::from([
      evolution_lane_trait_impl_row(&t1_key)
    ]))
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "T1-risky", p1.risky_impls.clone(), Vec::from([
      evolution_lane_trait_impl_row(&t1_key)
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("T1: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— T2: the same addition with the impl selecting step (review) ————
  let t2_key = t1_key.clone()
  let b2 = evolution_lane_trait_snapshot(t2_key.clone(), true, true)
  match trait_evolution_plan(&a1, &b2, t2_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p2) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "T2-verdict", p2.verdict.clone(), "review")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "T2-risky", p2.risky_impls.clone(), Vec::new())
  when Option::None then
    out.push("T2: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— T3: a removed method (review) ————
  let t3_key = "m::Tr#trait{run(let:Int)->Unit}".to_string()
  let a3 = evolution_lane_trait_snapshot(
    "m::Tr#trait{run(let:Int)->Unit,step(let:Int)->Unit}".to_string(), true, true)
  let b3 = evolution_lane_trait_snapshot(t3_key.clone(), true, true)
  match trait_evolution_plan(&a3, &b3, t3_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p3) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "T3-verdict", p3.verdict.clone(), "review")
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "T3-removed", p3.methods_removed.clone(), Vec::from([
      "step".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("T3: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— T4: no change (compatible) ————
  let t4_key = "m::Tr#trait{run(let:Int)->Unit}".to_string()
  let a4 = evolution_lane_trait_snapshot(t4_key.clone(), true, true)
  let b4 = evolution_lane_trait_snapshot(t4_key.clone(), true, true)
  match trait_evolution_plan(&a4, &b4, t4_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(p4) then
    evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "T4-verdict", p4.verdict.clone(), "compatible")
  when Option::None then
    out.push("T4: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— T5: a non-trait key -> None ————
  match trait_evolution_plan(&a4, &b4, "m::S#struct{}".to_string())
  when Option::Some(_) then
    out.push("T5: expected Option::None")
  when Option::None then ()
  end

  out
end

# The C1 capability fixture: A -> B, D -> A, E -> D (E is outside the
# analyzed program) and H -> B with an Unknown indirect call site.
def evolution_lane_capability_snapshot() -> SemanticSnapshot
  var s = delta_lane_snapshot()
  var syms: Vec[SemanticSymbol] = Vec::new()
  syms.push(delta_lane_fn_symbol("m::A#fn()->unit", "A", false))
  syms.push(delta_lane_fn_symbol("m::B#fn()->unit", "B", false))
  syms.push(delta_lane_fn_symbol("m::D#fn()->unit", "D", false))
  syms.push(delta_lane_fn_symbol("m::H#fn()->unit", "H", false))
  s.symbols = syms
  var calls: Vec[CallEdge] = Vec::new()
  calls.push(CallEdge {
    caller: delta_lane_sid("m::A#fn()->unit"),
    callee: delta_lane_sid("m::B#fn()->unit"),
    kind: CallEdgeKind::Direct
  })
  calls.push(CallEdge {
    caller: delta_lane_sid("m::D#fn()->unit"),
    callee: delta_lane_sid("m::A#fn()->unit"),
    kind: CallEdgeKind::Direct
  })
  calls.push(CallEdge {
    caller: delta_lane_sid("m::E#fn()->unit"),
    callee: delta_lane_sid("m::D#fn()->unit"),
    kind: CallEdgeKind::Direct
  })
  calls.push(CallEdge {
    caller: delta_lane_sid("m::H#fn()->unit"),
    callee: delta_lane_sid("m::B#fn()->unit"),
    kind: CallEdgeKind::Direct
  })
  s.calls = calls
  s.indirect_calls = Vec::from([
    IndirectCallEdge {
      caller: "m::H#fn()->unit".to_string(),
      site: "m::H#fn()->unit#B0#T".to_string(),
      signature: "fn()->unit".to_string(),
      candidates: Vec::new(),
      completeness: "Unknown".to_string()
    }
  ])
  s
end

# The C1 delta: B's effect row gains spawn + capability id "3", and B's
# capability edge cap1 toggles Absent -> Present.
def evolution_lane_capability_delta() -> SemanticDelta
  var d = semantic_delta_empty()
  var caps_after: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  caps_after.push("3".to_string())
  d.effect_delta = Vec::from([
    EffectDelta {
      function: "m::B#fn()->unit".to_string(),
      before: EffectSummaryView { bits: 0, capabilities: Vec::new() },
      after: EffectSummaryView { bits: 8, capabilities: caps_after }
    }
  ])
  d.capability_delta = Vec::from([
    CapabilityDelta {
      function: "m::B#fn()->unit".to_string(),
      capability: "cap1".to_string(),
      before: Presence::Absent,
      after: Presence::Present
    }
  ])
  d
end

def evolution_lane_capability_check() -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()

  # ———— C1: the transitive walk + the two blocked frontiers ————
  let s1 = evolution_lane_capability_snapshot()
  let d1 = evolution_lane_capability_delta()
  let p1 = capability_propagation_plan(&s1, &d1)
  evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "C1-verdict", p1.verdict.clone(), "review")
  evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "C1-changed", p1.changed.clone(), Vec::from([
    "m::B#fn()->unit".to_string(),
    "m::B#fn()->unit|cap1".to_string(),
    "m::B#fn()->unit|cap3".to_string()
  ]))
  evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "C1-propagated", p1.propagated_to.clone(), Vec::from([
    "m::A#fn()->unit".to_string(),
    "m::D#fn()->unit".to_string(),
    "m::E#fn()->unit".to_string(),
    "m::H#fn()->unit".to_string()
  ]))
  evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "C1-blocked", p1.blocked_at.clone(), Vec::from([
    "m::E#fn()->unit|external".to_string(),
    "m::H#fn()->unit|unknown-indirect:m::H#fn()->unit#B0#T".to_string()
  ]))

  # ———— C2: the empty delta (compatible, no rows) ————
  let p2 = capability_propagation_plan(&s1, semantic_delta_empty())
  evolution_lane_text(&mut out, "C2-verdict", p2.verdict.clone(), "compatible")
  evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "C2-changed", p2.changed.clone(), Vec::new())
  evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "C2-propagated", p2.propagated_to.clone(), Vec::new())
  evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "C2-blocked", p2.blocked_at.clone(), Vec::new())

  out
end

def evolution_lane_budget_check() -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()

  # ———— B1: the enum breaking plan's constraints (E2's shape) ————
  let e_key = "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int)}".to_string()
  let ea = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(
    "m::E#enum{A(int),B(int),C(int)}".to_string(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string(), "C".to_string()]), true, true, true, false)
  let eb = evolution_lane_enum_snapshot(e_key.clone(),
    Vec::from(["A".to_string(), "B".to_string()]), true, true, true, false)
  let ed = semantic_delta_of(&ea, &eb)
  match enum_evolution_plan(&eb, e_key.clone(), ed.clone())
  when Option::Some(ep) then
    let rows = evolution_plan_to_budget_constraints(EvolutionPlan::EnumPlan(ep))
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "B1-enum-constraints", rows, Vec::from([
      "allowed_abi_changes:m::E#enum{A(int),B(int)}".to_string(),
      "allowed_public_api_changes:m::E#enum{A(int),B(int)}".to_string(),
      "allowed_symbols:m::E#enum{A(int),B(int)}".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("B1: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— B2: the signature breaking plan's constraints (S5's shape) ————
  let s_key = "m::f#fn(let:Int)->Bool".to_string()
  let sa = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot("m::f#fn(let:Int)->Int".to_string(), false)
  let sb = evolution_lane_sig_snapshot(s_key.clone(), true)
  match signature_evolution_plan(&sa, &sb, s_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(sp) then
    let rows2 = evolution_plan_to_budget_constraints(EvolutionPlan::SignaturePlan(sp))
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "B2-signature-constraints", rows2, Vec::from([
      "allowed_abi_changes:m::f#fn(let:Int)->Bool".to_string(),
      "allowed_public_api_changes:m::f#fn(let:Int)->Bool".to_string(),
      "allowed_symbols:m::f#fn(let:Int)->Bool".to_string()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("B2: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— B3: the trait breaking plan's constraints (T1's shape) ————
  let t_key = "m::Tr#trait{run(let:Int)->Unit,step(let:Int)->Unit}".to_string()
  let ta = evolution_lane_trait_snapshot(
    "m::Tr#trait{run(let:Int)->Unit}".to_string(), true, true)
  let tb = evolution_lane_trait_snapshot(t_key.clone(), true, false)
  match trait_evolution_plan(&ta, &tb, t_key.clone())
  when Option::Some(tp) then
    let rows3 = evolution_plan_to_budget_constraints(EvolutionPlan::TraitPlan(tp))
    evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "B3-trait-constraints", rows3, Vec::from([
      "allowed_public_api_changes:" + t_key.clone(),
      "allowed_symbols:m::S#struct{}".to_string(),
      "allowed_symbols:" + t_key.clone()
    ]))
  when Option::None then
    out.push("B3: expected a plan")
  end

  # ———— B4: the capability plan's constraints admit the delta ————
  let cs = evolution_lane_capability_snapshot()
  let cd = evolution_lane_capability_delta()
  let cp = capability_propagation_plan(&cs, &cd)
  let rows4 = evolution_plan_to_budget_constraints(EvolutionPlan::CapabilityPlan(cp))
  let budget4 = evolution_budget_of_constraints(rows4.clone())
  evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "B4-capability-constraints", rows4, Vec::from([
    "allowed_capability_additions:m::B#fn()->unit|cap1".to_string(),
    "allowed_capability_additions:m::B#fn()->unit|cap3".to_string(),
    "allowed_effect_additions:m::B#fn()->unit".to_string(),
    "allowed_symbols:m::B#fn()->unit".to_string()
  ]))
  evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "B4-budget-empty", budget_verify(&budget4, &cd), Vec::new())
  # Fail-closed twin: the default empty budget rejects the same delta.
  evolution_lane_bool(&mut out, "B4-empty-budget-rejects",
    !budget_verify(&ChangeBudget {}, &cd).is_empty())

  # ———— B5: the delta-refined family rows -> budget -> budget_verify ————
  var ep5 = EnumEvolutionPlan {
    type_key: e_key.clone(),
    verdict: "compatible".to_string()
  }
  match enum_evolution_plan(&eb, e_key.clone(), ed.clone())
  when Option::Some(p5) then ep5 = p5
  when Option::None then ()
  end
  var plans: Vec[EvolutionPlan] = Vec::new()
  plans.push(EvolutionPlan::EnumPlan(ep5))
  let rows5 = evolution_plans_to_budget_constraints(plans, Option::Some(ed.clone()))
  let budget5 = evolution_budget_of_constraints(rows5)
  evolution_lane_keys(&mut out, "B5-refined-budget", budget_verify(&budget5, &ed), Vec::new())

  out
end

# Run every sub-lane; the returned list names every mismatch (empty = the
# whole lane verifies). Exported for a behavior lane.
pub def semantic_evolution_lane_check() -> Vec[String]
  var out: Vec[String] = Vec::new()
  for row in evolution_lane_enum_check() do
    out.push(row)
  end
  for row2 in evolution_lane_signature_check() do
    out.push(row2)
  end
  for row3 in evolution_lane_trait_check() do
    out.push(row3)
  end
  for row4 in evolution_lane_capability_check() do
    out.push(row4)
  end
  for row5 in evolution_lane_budget_check() do
    out.push(row5)
  end
  out
end
